hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"15949","Abu Mu'awiya narrated to us, he said, al-A'mash narrated to us, from Sallam ibn Shurahbil, from Habba and Sawa the two sons of Khalid, they said: We entered upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was mending something, so we helped him. So he said: Do not despair of provision so long as your heads shake, for man is born of his mother red with no skin upon him, then Allah the Mighty and Majestic provides for him."
"15950","Waki' narrated to us, he said, al-A'mash narrated to us, from Sallam Abu Shurahbil, he said: I heard Habba and Sawa the two sons of Khalid say: We came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was doing work or building a building, so we helped him with it. When he finished, he supplicated for us and said: Do not despair of good so long as your heads shake. Man is born of his mother red with no skin upon him, then Allah gives him and provides for him."
"15952","Affan narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, he said, Khalid narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Shaqiq, from Abd Allah ibn Abi al-Jad'a: that he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There shall enter Paradise through the intercession of a man of my umma more than Banu Tamim. So they said: O Messenger of Allah, other than you? He said: Other than me, other than me. I said: Did you hear it yourself from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: I heard it myself."
